# Everything under data/ is rebuilt from the sibling projects and stays out of
# git -- EXCEPT data/manual/, the human decision files, which are
# version-controlled and never machine-overwritten (CLAUDE.md rule 4,
# docs/ENTITY_RESOLUTION.md).
#
# Written as data/* rather than data/ because git will not re-include a path
# inside a wholly excluded directory: the negation is only reachable if the
# directory itself was never excluded.
data/*
!data/manual/
data/manual/*
!data/manual/*.csv

venv/

# Claude Code local-only state: this machine's session lock, its worktrees,
# and settings.local.json (permission choices made in this session). Not
# .claude/launch.json or .claude/settings.json -- those are project config
# worth sharing if this repo ever commits them.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/*.lock

# The published page and its lazily-fetched index. Built by build_site.py
# (and build/export_fec.py for fec_rows.json), deployed by
# ne-connect-nightly.yml as a Pages artifact -- not served from this tree
# since the Pages source moved to build_type=workflow on 2026-09-20.
# Committing them would only bloat history (d/fec_rows.json is ~50MB and
# GitHub hard-rejects any file over 100MB). Rebuild locally with the two
# scripts; they create d/ themselves.
/index.html
/d/

# Local-only tools (docs/PRIVACY.md): pipeline/review.html embeds the entire
# unreviewed review_queue.csv verbatim, including every individual x
# individual name-collision guess. ne-connect-nightly.yml stages this whole
# checkout as the Pages artifact (its rsync excludes pipeline/ as a second
# guard), so a committed pipeline/ would be one exclude away from publishing
# the raw, unreviewed candidate list right alongside the finished site --
# this must never be committed, only generated locally on demand by
# build/build_review_tool.py.
pipeline/
